CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^.*error.*$
--
C++20 requires-expression soft-failure ([expr.prim.req.general]/5): a
requirement whose expression is invalid in the immediate context makes the
requires-expression evaluate to false rather than ill-forming the program, even
when the invalid expression uses an overloaded operator on a class type
(`a + a` with no operator+) or a member access on a non-class type
(`a.foo()`).  Guards routing requirement nodes to SFINAE-guarded evaluation
before the ordinary operand recursion can emit a hard diagnostic.  See
doc/architectural/cpp-requires-expression-support.md.
